  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nA social request authenticated before its API token was revoked could still succeed because `AuthedUser` discarded token identity. The new regression reproduced HTTP 200 where 401 was required. Retain the internal token ID and revalidate current token owner, purpose, activity and account eligibility under transaction locks through each protected social operation. The same account's independent active session remains usable.\n\nDepends on **#377**, with the existing social stack beneath it. Account-only pilot; legacy messaging, delegated entities and global-role revocation remain incomplete. No client contract or schema change.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Executable TLA+/TLC model: 7,464 distinct states; safety and fair progress pass. Three unsafe variants each produce the required authority counterexample.\n- 64 cases generated from actual checked Read outcomes. Native PostgreSQL HTTP/guard suite: **82 examples, zero failures**, including both revocation/write race orders, shared reads and password-reset lock order.\n- Pre-fix handler: **73 examples, one failure**, expected 401 / actual 200. Same regression passes with the handler guard restored.\n- CI external-database adapter also passes 82 examples locally; refuses wrong-name and populated databases before fixture DDL.\n- Fixture-only paired overhead: added warm p95 **4.841 ms**, below the predeclared 20 ms limit. No production/high-degree claim.\n- Workflow/scope tests: 21 passed. Full new Stack backend build passed: **2,542 examples, zero failures**, application executable built, exit 0. [Full CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35011441934) and [social CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35011441891) passed at current `80cd4a1a4b928d6cb4252bfabc30a404be7b937b`, including the real PostgreSQL 17 HTTP/session step. The catalog audit is also green after explicitly classifying internal lock modes; its gate was unchanged.\n\nModel bounds, command/version details, traceability and logs: [`docs/social/session-boundary.md`](docs/social/session-boundary.md). Most added lines are generated model graph and actual evidence; core enforcement is one small shared helper.\n\n## Flags, migration and rollback\n\nNo migration/backfill; internal synthetic auth constructors explicitly carry no token identity. Existing test assertions retained. `SOCIAL_V2_ENABLED`, database runtime and web flags remain inactive in production. Before activation, reverting preserves database writes and contracts. After activation, retain this enforcement version: rolling back to a handler that ignores revoked sessions would restore the demonstrated bypass.\n\nDraft, unmerged; no deployment command or production activation. Existing branch-scoped Vercel suppression and `[CF-Pages-Skip]` retained. Earlier automatic provider deployment exceptions remain documented in the handoff and are not claimed resolved.\n\n\n## Parent reconciliation \u2014 2026-09-16\n\nNormal merge `2be39150f626dcd5181951532a8ebe25a3ce3fa4` preserves original head `80cd4a1a4b928d6cb4252bfabc30a404be7b937b` and current parent `3606fb5c2215e00b1f3661abdf9e969231ac3b36`. No shared history was rewritten. Social runtime, SQL, models, tests and social workflow remain byte-identical to the original head. Previously merged artwork and Instagram changes from the parent remain intact; catalog outputs were regenerated with the unchanged strict policy.\n\nVerified locally on the reconciled tree: 82 PostgreSQL HTTP/session examples, zero failures, including both token-revocation race orders; positive session model (7,464 states) and three expected unsafe counterexamples; 21 CI workflow/scope tests; strict catalog JSON and CSV, including the preserved session-lock decision. All final commands exited 0. Initial environment setup failures were retained in the audit evidence; no assertions, timeouts or gates were changed.\n\nNew exact-head hosted checks and any renewed review remain required. Existing feature and migration activation gates are unchanged. No manual deployment was performed. Native-stack integration remains separately blocked by its linear-history requirement; this update does not claim the stack is merged.\n",
